# Architecture stays "all" here: the GitHub release, the R2 apt pool and its
# installers all name sysmanage_<v>-1_all.deb.  Only the Launchpad upload
# switches it to "any" (build-and-release.yml deploy-launchpad), so each PPA
# architecture builds its own package and riscv64 can carry its wheels.
Package: sysmanage
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${riscv64:Depends},
 python3 (>= 3.10),
 python3-pip,
 python3-venv,
 python3-dev,
 libpq-dev,
 gcc,
 adduser,
 systemd,
 nodejs (>= 18),
 nginx
Recommends: postgresql (>= 12),
 xorriso,
 docker.io
Suggests: postgresql-client,
 sysmanage-canary
Description: Centralized system management server
 SysManage is a comprehensive system management platform that provides:
  * Centralized agent management
  * System monitoring and metrics
  * Package management across multiple systems
  * Security policy enforcement
  * Certificate management
  * Firewall configuration
  * User access control
  * Web-based administration interface
 .
 This package installs the SysManage server which manages connected
 agents. It requires a PostgreSQL database (can be on a separate host).
 .
 After installation, configure /etc/sysmanage.yaml to point to your
 PostgreSQL database. Use the online config builder at:
 https://sysmanage.org/config-builder.html

Package: sysmanage-canary
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 python3 (>= 3.10),
 python3-yaml,
 python3-psycopg,
 adduser,
 systemd
Description: Outside watcher for a SysManage server
 sysmanage-canary checks a SysManage server from the outside -- the web
 console, the backend API, the database, the network, and whether agents are
 still reporting -- and sends email when something stops working.  It runs
 as its own service and user with its own configuration
 (/etc/sysmanage-canary.yaml), on the system Python, so it keeps working when
 the server, its virtualenv or its database has failed.  It can run on the
 server itself or, better, on another machine.
